orus.traineddata
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright 2025 Anastasya Bogdanova, Iskra Project
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    https://github.com/AButon-8/iskra_ocr
    https://rpubs.com/AButon/orus_tesseract

A fine-tune of tesseract's Russian model for pre-reform orthography, trained on
the social-democratic newspaper «Искра» (1900–1905).

`orus.traineddata` is not distributed here; it is an input you supply.
`tools/build_orusd.sh` is what uses it, and it:

  - copies its `lstm` (11775283 bytes), `lstm-unicharset` (9360 bytes) and
    `lstm-recoder` (1201 bytes) into `orusd.traineddata` byte for byte;
  - adds a `lstm-word-dawg` compiled from the ru_petr1708 word list below;
  - adds a `lstm-punc-dawg` and `lstm-number-dawg` recompiled from stock
    `rus.traineddata`.

Nothing is retrained. The recogniser in `orusd` is the orus recogniser
unchanged; only the dictionary components are new. This paragraph is the
statement of changes required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b).

`tools/build_ru_petr1708.sh` writes a second, different derivative, and here
the recogniser is modified. `ru-petr1708.traineddata` contains:

  - an `lstm` (11791699 bytes) that is the orus network fine-tuned, not
    copied. Training continued from the orus weights with `lstmtraining` for
    7400 iterations over synthetic renderings of pre-reform text, at a
    positive:negative line ratio of 1:10. Every weight in the network is
    liable to have changed. The topology is unaltered
    (`Lfys64 → Lfx96 → Lrx96 → Lfx512 → O1c1`) and the final layer was widened
    from 133 to 137 outputs;
  - an `lstm-unicharset` (9658 bytes) extended from orus's 133 characters to
    137 by the addition of Ѳ ѳ Ѵ ѵ — fita and izhitsa. The first 133 entries
    are unchanged in content and in index order, and the `lstm-recoder`
    (1237 bytes) is rebuilt to match;
  - the same three dawgs, compiled afresh against the 137-entry unicharset.

The purpose of the fine-tune is that orus cannot represent fita or izhitsa at
all, so it cannot emit them whatever dictionary it is given. Adding the four
characters is the whole of the change. This paragraph and the list above are
the statement of changes required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b) for
`ru-petr1708.traineddata`. The training text was generated from the
ru_petr1708 word list below.


